#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
bd-pool-autobalancer — Autonomous Cross-Pool Quota Load-Balancer & Failover Daemon (O1740 / O1789 Swarm #7)

Continuously monitors:
  - /home/mboyle/bd-persist/POOL_STATE.tsv (state, five_hour_pct, weekly_pct, resets_at)
  - Live health of codex, kimi, AGY, and local-4xt4 (10.0.70.164:4010 GPU Orchestrator & 10.0.70.228:4000 LiteLLM)

Implements O1740 Dynamic Capability Routing + Autonomous Failover:
  - --recommend <role> [--json] [--simulate-claude-exhausted]
      * Command Squad (integrator, dispatch, audit, adjudicator, trainer, lensrouter, pm):
        Picks the OK Opus-tier pool (A, B, C, D) with the lowest five_hour_pct (tie-break: lowest weekly_pct,
        then role affinity). If all Claude pools are >=85% or OFF-PACE/LIMITED/UNKNOWN, fails over cleanly to
        codex (gpt-6-astra) or hermes (mimo-v2.6-pro-1024b / glm-5.3-753b).
      * Heavy Lifters (worker, builder, fixer, review-*):
        Picks the most capable admitting pool (five_hour_pct < 80%), balancing load across Claude ABCD
        (claude-opus-5-5), Codex (gpt-6-sol / gpt-6-astra), Kimi (kimi-for-coding), and Local 4xT4
        (qwen3-coder-30b-a3b / swift-qwen3.8-flash-next).
      * Lightweight Investigators (investigator, probe, cavecrew-*):
        Picks the fast-model pool with the highest idle quota (max(100 - five_hour_pct)) or Local Tier 1
        (qwen3-coder-30b-a3b at $0 marginal cost).
  - --status [--json] [--no-color]
      Prints a rich, color-coded table of all pools (A, B, C, D, codex, kimi, AGY, local-4xt4), current
      5h/weekly %, headroom before 80% soft cap, and recommended routing per role tier.
  - --daemon [--interval 30]
      Continuously refreshes /var/tmp/bd-pool-autobalancer.json every 30s.
"""

